  "workload": "Per size: 20 fixed queries x 20 repeats, 5 closed-loop request workers; plus 20 first-execution, 20 warm-up and one high-frequency gap request. Every request starts independent page/count CQP calls, for up to 5 page plus 5 background count processes.",
  "scheduling": "The request worker submits exact count to a distinct 5-worker pool and executes page immediately, then waits for count before admitting its next request. Count completion is measured from the same request start, including queue delay; actual time overlap is recorded, not inferred from configuration.",
  "count_publication": "Page result contains null total_hits/matched_segments/matched_documents and pending status. The benchmark publishes completed exact counts only after joining the count future. A count may physically finish before page delivery; those cases are recorded separately.",
  "correctness": "For every request, token spans and every KWIC field equal an unbounded full-result reference. Reference page hashes also equal the retained historical baseline; complete counts independently verified by raw template enumeration. Separate hand gold checks multi-sentence documents, nested endpoints, duplicate OR, Unicode, non-first/empty pages and missing structure errors.",
  "subset": "The combined page/count candidate explicitly rejects paragraph scope. It requires a trusted index recipe with complete sentence/document structural coverage. The scale recipe uses p as document; the small gold corpus uses separate doc and multiple sentences.",
  "limitations": [
    "No deployed business API, production authorization or durable job scheduler is measured.",
    "Fresh processes and first-execution observations are not cold-disk measurements; OS page cache was not cleared.",
    "Parent/cgroup peak memory includes prior full-dump correctness preparation; per-CQP child RSS is reported separately.",
    "New experiment disk peak is sampled at 0.25s and excludes reused baseline files; it is not a strict absolute peak.",
    "Sequential shared-host measurements are not formal dedicated-hardware acceptance. Original 3s ordinary first-page, 30s ordinary complete-count and 120s high-frequency count thresholds remain unchanged."
